<title>JAPAN: Japan end-March coffee stocks up 26.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan end-March coffee stocks up 26.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese warehouse coffee stocks totalled 67,030 tonnes at the end of March, up by 26.7 percent from a year earlier, the Agriculture Ministry said.</p>
<p>At the end of March 1996, stocks in Japan, the world's third-biggest coffee consumer after the United States and Germany, were 52,899 tonnes, the ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Details of the coffee stocks were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Mar 97	  Feb 97	Mar 96</p>
<p> Brazil	     14,187	  14,862	11,050</p>
<p> Colombia	   14,669	  14,314	13,239</p>
<p> Indonesia	  11,051	  10,420	 9,228</p>
<p> Central America  15,171	  13,640	 8,478</p>
<p> Others	     11,952	  12,121	10,904</p>
<p> Total		67,030	  65,357	52,899</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
